Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
we're going to begin with a growing  pressure on new york's governor andrew  cuomo to resign  after a long-awaited report detailing  numerous allegations of sexual  harassment  cuomo continues to deny that he  intentionally did anything wrong  investigators allege he sexually  harassed 11 women many of them young  and retaliated against at least one  staffer who came forward  now the accusations include unwelcome  and non-consensual touching  offensive remarks and sexual comments  our national correspondent that's tariqa  duncan has been following this story for  months  and joins us from albany as you know the  state capital of new york  tariqa good morning to you a lot of  people want the governor to step down  including president biden but he  seems he seems to be doubling down what  else do you know about the story  well for starters gail we know that the  governor as  it seems at this hour has no plans to  leave now this  investigation was led by two independent  attorneys that were appointed by the  attorney general's  office and it didn't just talk about  sexual harassment in this report  but it spoke of a culture that was  filled with fear and intimidation  that the report says allowed sexual  harassment to occur  and persist this investigation has  revealed conduct that corrodes  the very fabric and character of our  state government  the explosive 165-page report  based on interviews with 179 people  alleges new york governor andrew cuomo  created a hostile work environment for  women  the independence investigation found  that governor cuomo sexually harassed  multiple women many of whom were young  women  by engaging in unwanted groping  kisses hugging and by making  inappropriate comments  eleven women came forward and  investigators say they found all of them  credible  including a new york state trooper who  worked on cuomo's security detail  the report says he sexually harassed her  on a number of occasions  by running his hand across her stomach  from her belly button to her hip running  his finger down her back  and making sexually suggestive comments  our investigation revealed  that these were not isolated incidents  they were part of a pattern another  woman  identified as executive assistant number  one  said the governor groped her according  to the report in november the governor  hugged her and reached under her blouse  and grabbed her breasts while at the  executive mansion  i want you to know directly from me  that i never touched anyone  inappropriately  or made inappropriate sexual advances  in a pre-recorded statement the governor  defended himself against all of the  allegations  the facts are much different than what  has been  portrayed the governor also showed  photos hugging and kissing people of all  genders claiming  that's how he conveys warmth i now  understand  that there are generational or  cultural perspectives that frankly  i hadn't fully appreciated  and i have learned from this i think  that the governor is in for  a lot of litigation civilly perhaps  something criminally though we don't  know that yet  cbs news legal analyst ricky clement the  attorney general was very clear  that she did her job her job is over  and it is up to any police department  any district attorney's office if they  see  any of these allegations to go forward  if they choose to do so  the leader of the state assembly a  democrat said  the governor is no longer should be in  office at this time and said that they  would move quickly as lawmakers to  complete  its impeachment inquiry meanwhile that  groping allegation is being investigated  by police  and the district attorney here in albany  has also opened a criminal investigation  anthony jerica thank you charlotte  bennett was the governor's former  executive assistant  and was among the first to come forward  and accuse him  of inappropriate conduct in her  exclusive interview with nora o'donnell  bennett talked about what justice would  look like to her  the new york attorney general said  multiple times today that she believes  you  and the other women mentioned in this  report what does that mean to you  it was extremely validating and i feel  vindicated  um it's been a long day but  i'm i'm proud to be a new yorker right  now  the governor said today that he accepts  responsibility  and that he's making changes do you  believe him  accepting responsibility means stepping  down  and not only is he not stepping down but  he's outright denying the things that  he did so i don't believe him and i  don't want an apology  it's not necessary it's fake and his  propaganda video was not only  uncomfortable and inappropriate but  downright weird  and unnecessary in addition to this  investigation that found that the  governor sexually harassed  multiple women they also found  that the governor and his aides created  a toxic  work environment that enabled sexual  harassment  is that consistent with what you  experienced it's  extremely consistent and i think the  environment of  fear the environment of humiliation  the idea that at any moment you feel  like you could either lose your job or  get screamed at  or you know it was traumatic  on its own so when the most powerful  person in the office  and also the most powerful person in the  state  acts inappropriately you think  why would anyone take that seriously or  think that i deserve any respect in this  office  gonna be an interesting situation for  the governor now who seems not ready to  resign at this point  no but it's such a steady drumbeat of  calls to resign that's why  i'm curious to see how all this is going  to play out but he insists  he didn't do anything wrong so he's not  stepping down but you've got the  president you've got two senators  i agree with charlotte bennett about the  video i'm really wondering about the  wisdom of that video i just don't think  that was helpful it appears they  were prepared for it and in a way i mean  we know from  reporting that the governor was  interviewed for 11 hours by  investigators i'm anticipating after  that he saw what was coming  and prepared the video and nora we'll  have more coverage tonight on the cbs  evening news

